DTEND:20260605T190000Z
SUMMARY:"Shepherdstown Live" First Friday Music - for ALL Ages!
ORGANIZATION:Experience Shepherdstown
LOCATION:Shepherdstown - TBD
DESCRIPTION:<p>_Community\n_FAMILY FRIENDLY\nEnjoy free live outdoor music on First Fridays in May-October on the lawn of McMurran Hall\, in downtown Shepherdstown. Bring your friends/family\, a chair or blanket\, and stay after the music to dine\, shop and play! Today's band Tony M Music!\nBring the kids and join us in town FREE live music\, games\, and lots of kid-oriented fun!\nTony is a former elementary school teacher with 11 years of experience teaching grades 1\, 3\, and 4\, and five years as a behavioral coach for grades 3–5. Since 2014\, he has been a full-time professional musician\, performing over 175 shows annually at schools\, libraries\, and family events. He also leads workshops for educators on integrating music into the classroom.\nA songwriter since 2003\, Tony now performs original\, interactive programs that blend music\, literature\, and storytelling while promoting positive mental health and a growth mindset. His earliest live performances were in 2001/2002 on the steps of Knutti Hall and at The Meck Open Mic!\nAs with every First Friday\, shops will be open late. Come enjoy Shepherdstown's music\, unique shopping\, great food and good company!\nShepherdstown LIVE is co-sponsored by the Town of Shepherdstown\, Jefferson Security Bank\, Stoney's Pub\, Nikki Visions Vol 1 and Wind Gap Music. Brought to you by Experience Shepherdstown.\n\n<b>Location Details:</b> Shepherdstown - TBD\n\n<b>Contact Info:</b> Shannon Thomas 6513297063 shanpur@gmail.com</p
CATEGORIES:Community & Civic, Music & Film & Stage
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SOURCE:shepherdstown.info
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
