SUMMARY:Mid-day Soiree at Falling Spring
ORGANIZATION:Falling Spring Property
LOCATION:Falling Spring Property
DESCRIPTION:<p>Join PVAS for its annual spring fundraiser event\, this year at Falling Spring\, the historic property where the Bee Line March of 1775 started. This beautiful historic home was built in 1837 and is on the National Register of Historic Places in West Virginia.\nEnjoy home tours by local historians\, self-guided walks down to Bubbling Spring\, and lawn games at the home of Ed and Lorri Schwartz. Light fare and libations will be served indoors and on the porch.\nIt will be held rain or shine\, so please dress casually.\nTicket prices are as follows:\n$75- Individual\n$200- Donor (admits 2)\n$275- Supporter (admits 2)\n$350- Patron (admits 2)\nParking and other details will be emailed to guests prior to the event. Please RSVP by May 20.\n\n<b>Location Details:</b> Falling Spring Property\, 142 Falling Spring Rd\, Shepherdstown\, WV\, 25443\n\n<b>Contact Info:</b> Ellen Kinzer 681-252-1387 ellen@potomacaudubon.org</p
CATEGORIES:Uncategorized
URL:https://www.potomacaudubon.org/event/mid-day-soiree/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SOURCE:shepherdstown.info
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
